A||||3||Thecrewchief1||Fiero quit running||||1||
Z||000000||Thecrewchief1||04-02-2001||01:23 AM||||Well heres my won't run story. On my way over the Skyway bridge in St Pete, my 86 GT just quit running and there I was on the side of the road. The engine would turn over but wouldn't fire. Triple A came and got the car and towed it back home. I had a new Accel coil and module and new cap and rotor with new AC Rapid Fire spark plugs. Sunday morning I tried to start it but it wouldn't fire, I then replaced the cap, rotor, and coil with the old stuff, but no fire. I then replaced the module with the old one and the car started right up! So I jumped in to go for a ride, for about 3 miles. When I jumped on it pulling out of the store parking lot, I got up to about 50 and the motor just shut down again. Tried to start it, no fire. Triple A again back to my shop where we think the problem is the pick up in the dist is burning out the modules, any thoughts? The old dist is a reman from 94 by the date code, not a delco. I am putting a new dist in it the morning, I hope this does it!!  Thanks Bill||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||04-02-2001||01:30 AM||||It sounds like you've covered all the bases.  It is a good idea to carry a spare coil and ignition module (and tools), just in case that happens again.  I've gone through a few coils on road trips and carrying a spare was a life saver.<P>If the rest of the distributor looked OK, I would just replace the pickup coil......why replace the whole thing.  A pick up coil is $1o......a distributor is over $100.   Just a thought.<P>Let us know if that cures your problem. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-02-2001||02:46 AM||||Pick-up coils get crackes in the wire sleeving when they get old. Mine did the same thing. I yanked the distributor and replaced everything. No problems since!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cozmo||04-02-2001||07:41 AM||||Good diagnosis.  I always carry spare ignition stuff just in case.  A known good set of parts can make troubleshooting much easier.  I see you are from Pinellas Park, there is an excellent club (Suncoast Fieros) local to you.  Email me for more info and welcome to the forum, Bill!<P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 2M6 Targa<BR>'86 GT<BR>'87 Coupe||||reg||1
